From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:15:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 26/28] freedreno/a2xx: Xenos fetches 8- and 16-bit vertex
 formats; read env hooks once

Each vertex attribute has its own fetch constant, so each gets its own endian
swap: 8in32 for 32-bit components, 8in16 for 16-bit ones, none for bytes.
That allows k_8_8_8_8, k_16_16 and k_16_16_16_16 (and the 16-bit float ones),
the vertex formats Xenia lists. glamor's GL_SHORT positions went through
u_vbuf, which read the VBO back through the write-combined mapping and
translated it on every draw.

x11perf: rect10 334k -> 2.85M, aa10text 185k -> 811k, aa24text 150k -> 512k,
oddtilerect100 117k -> 246k, copywinwin10 15k -> 19k. dEQP vertex_arrays,
draw, attribute_location, default_vertex_attrib: 769/769 pass.

The experiment hooks (XENOS_INTERP, XENOS_FULL_RESOLVE, XENOS_FLUSH_BARRIER,
XENOS_DEBUG, FD2_DUMP_SHADERS, FD2_DEBUG_FETCH) are read once: getenv per
draw and per batch showed up in profiles.

